Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 23:41:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00890/11362] [outer-loop] On-policy result: MiniCPM5-1B
 UNSUITABLE base (5% own-correct, 71% gen-trunc)

First real on-policy run (no-think). Honest read via instrumentation: own_sample_correct_rate
=0.05 (MiniCPM generates only 5% correct-AND-complete traces; gen_truncation 0.71 -- verbose
reasoning model rambles past 1024 even no-think) -> almost NO bootstrap data. TRUNCATION_
INVALID: trained arms truncate 13-30% in eval (base 0.0) because training on the 71%-truncated
own-traces taught WORSE stopping. True base no-think acc=0.23 (the 0.49 was thinking-mode
truncation-corruption). gold_control_ok=True (LoRA didn't forget). CONCLUSION: this is a
MODEL-SUITABILITY finding -- MiniCPM5-1B is a verbose reasoning model unfit for on-policy RFT
on GSM8K. Need a base with CONCISE terminating answers + decent completion (own-correct >>5%,
gen-trunc <~10%). Instrumentation caught a 4th silent failure tonight; the verifier question
remains untested pending a suitable base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
